# Research module: market-data CSVs are local fixtures, not for git.
#
# Note the trailing /* rather than a bare directory: git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so a bare `research/data/` would make the negation
# below unreachable.
#
# The carve-out is a dependency argument, not a size one. Broker OHLCV is not
# durably reproducible -- Pepperstone revises bars, backfills gaps and retains
# finite history -- so a file that is only hashed cannot be restored once lost,
# and any parity claim resting on it becomes permanently uncheckable rather
# than merely stale. XAUUSD_H1.csv underpins T9a and the seq=31 flood_tide
# artifact, so it must be recoverable, not merely verifiable. At H1 that costs
# 6.2 MB.
#
# Everything else stays ignored and is pinned by research/data_manifest.json,
# relocatable via QH_DATA_DIR. Bulk series need their own off-disk archive: a
# checksum on a file that exists in exactly one place is a detection mechanism
# with nothing behind it.
research/data/*
!research/data/XAUUSD_H1.csv
